WEBVTT

00:00:05.054 --> 00:00:08.940
The neurodiverse population remains
a largely untapped pool of talent.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.221
Unemployment runs as high as 80%.

00:00:13.283 --> 00:00:17.322
Even when they're working, highly capable,
neurodiverse people are often

00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:18.980
underemployed.

00:00:19.127 --> 00:00:21.786
Many times, despite
having required skill sets and

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.780
solid credentials, they
have to settle for menial jobs.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.210
These poor numbers are
due to the way companies

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:31.104
screen and hire their
possible candidates.

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:37.046
Fostering an inclusive workplace begins
with making neurodiversity a priority.

00:00:38.257 --> 00:00:42.760
Employers and recruiters need to revamp
their hiring practices so as not to miss

00:00:42.761 --> 00:00:46.120
out on any of the neurodiverse talent
that could help the company flourish.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:50.800
Recruitment of people on the 
spectrum is only the first step.

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:55.050
Employers need to make certain
accommodations for a fulfilling work

00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:57.200
environment for people
across the spectrum.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:03.355
Encouraging neurodiversity makes
organizations inclusive and innovative.

00:01:04.754 --> 00:01:07.698
Employees who identify on
the neurodiverse spectrum

00:01:07.699 --> 00:01:10.221
bring with them new
ways of looking at things.

00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:14.600
This encourages the entire 
team to think creatively.

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:19.580
Merging unique perspectives and ideas
within a team naturally fosters an

00:01:19.581 --> 00:01:22.453
environment that is innovative 
and forward-thinking.